SUMMARY:Nate Jackson: Big Dog Tour LIVE at Blue Note Hawaii (Early Show)
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. \nAbout the Performer\nNate Jackson is one of the fastest-rising stars in stand-up comedy\, boasting over 4.5 million TikTok followers and more than 700 million global views across his viral content. Known for his electric stage presence\, sharp crowd work\, and fearless approach to taboo topics\, Jackson has been selling out theaters across the U.S. on his BIG DOG TOUR. \nIn 2025\, Nate released his first one-hour Netflix special\, Nate Jackson: Super Funny\, which premiered at #3 on the Netflix Top 10. His comedy seamlessly blends masterfully crafted material with his unique style of hilarious crowd work — diving into subjects others won’t touch and leaving audiences in stitches from start to finish. \nBeyond stand-up\, Nate is currently shooting Season 2 of Apple TV+’s Bad Monkey and has appeared in the Lionsgate feature Good Fortune alongside Keanu Reeves\, Seth Rogen\, and Keke Palmer. He has also made memorable appearances on Curb Your Enthusiasm (HBO)\, Spirited (Apple TV+)\, and Kevin Hart’s Hart of the City (Comedy Central). \nEvent Details\n\nDate: Wednesday\, July 8\, 2026\nTime: 6:30 PM HST (Doors open at 5:00 PM)\nVenue: Blue Note Hawaii\, 2335 Kalakaua Avenue\, Honolulu\, HI 96815\nShow Duration: Approximately 90 minutes\nAge Restrictions: 18+ with valid ID\nFood/Beverage Minimum: $20 per person\nHosted by: Trenton Cotten\, featuring Pepper Lamb\n\nAbout the Venue\nBlue Note Hawaii is Honolulu’s premier intimate live entertainment venue\, located at 2335 Kalakaua Avenue in the heart of Waikiki. Part of the legendary Blue Note brand\, this world-class venue offers a unique combination of exceptional live performances and a full-service dining experience in an intimate\, club-style setting. \nThe venue features communal-style seating that is first come\, first served — so arriving early is highly recommended for the best seats. A full dinner menu and full bar are available throughout the show\, with a $20 food or beverage minimum per person. The intimate atmosphere means every seat feels close to the stage\, creating an electric connection between performer and audience. \nBlue Note Hawaii has hosted some of the biggest names in comedy and music\, and its Waikiki location makes it one of the most sought-after entertainment destinations in Hawaii. The venue’s warm\, club-style ambiance creates an unforgettable backdrop for a night of world-class stand-up comedy. \nWhat to Expect\nThis is the early show of two performances on July 8 — Nate Jackson is performing two shows per night across July 8 and 9\, giving fans multiple opportunities to catch the Big Dog Tour in Honolulu. The show features Nate headlining with host Trenton Cotten and special guest Pepper Lamb opening the night. \nExpect a high-energy\, laugh-out-loud evening of stand-up comedy featuring Nate’s signature blend of sharp material and crowd interaction. His fearless approach to comedy and undeniable charisma make every show a unique\, electric experience. Arrive early to secure the best seats and enjoy dinner before the show begins. \nThis is a 18+ event. Seating is communal and first come\, first served\, so plan to arrive well before the 6:30 PM showtime to get settled with food and drinks. \nTicket Information\nPrice Range: $30 – $50 (plus fees; resale prices may vary) \nPurchase official tickets through TicketWeb (a Ticketmaster company)\, or find resale tickets through VividSeats for flexible options including pairs and premium seating. \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/nate-jackson-big-dog-tour-live-at-blue-note-hawaii-wednesday-early/
